We anticipate that losses will continue for the foreseeable future. At December 31, 2017, our accumulated deficit was approximately $712.4 million. Our actual cash requirements may vary materially from those planned because of a number of factors including:
• Changes in the focus, direction and pace of our development programs;
• Competitive and technical advances;
• Costs associated with the development of our product candidates;
• Our ability to secure partnering arrangements;
• Costs of filing, prosecuting, defending and enforcing any patent claims and any other intellectual property rights, or other developments; and
• Other matters identified under Part I – Item 1A. “Risk Factors.”
Working capital as of December 31, 2017 was $69.9 million, consisting of $90.8 million in current assets and $20.9 million in current liabilities. Working capital as of December 31, 2016 was $89.1 million, consisting of $104.9 million in current assets and $15.8 million in current liabilities.
